// error
// #6025: a nested slice literal `[[1], ["a"]]` — the outer list's own two
// elements ([]i64` and `[]string`) disagree, which `vSliceLitJoin`'s outer
// pass catches with no special recursion needed (each nested list is
// internally consistent; only their OWN inferred types differ). The
// recursive half of the same function covers the complementary shape, an
// outer list whose elements' inferred types agree while ONE of them is
// internally inconsistent (`[[1, "a"], [2, 3]]`, both defaulting to `[]i64`
// from their own first element) — not pinned here since it reports on the
// same E0041 code and text shape as this case, one level down.
fn main() {
  let x = [[1], ["a"]]
  print("${len(x)}\n")
}
